{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Only that there shall be no needy among you.</b> Yet further on it says ״כִּי לֹא יֶחְדַּל אֶבְיוֹן״? Rather: when you do the will of the Omnipresent, there are needy among others but not among you; and when you do not do the will of the Omnipresent, there are needy among you." "<b>Needy.</b> Destitute compared to a poor man; and the term אֶבְיוֹן — that he desires everything (see Leviticus Rabbah 34)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:10.133607913Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}